# Who wrote what.
#
# This repository's history was split out of MetaMeld with `git subtree
# split`, so it carries that repository's identities: the GitHub web UI, two
# differently-configured Macs, and Claude Code sessions running in the cloud.
# They are all the same person. This file tells git so -- `git log`,
# `git shortlog` and `git blame` read it and collapse the list.
#
# It changes how history is *displayed*, not the history itself. Nothing is
# rewritten, no commit hash moves, and anyone who has already cloned is
# unaffected. (GitHub's own contributor graph ignores .mailmap; this fixes
# the command line and most tooling, which is where it is worth fixing.)
#
# The canonical form is the GitHub account plus GitHub's noreply address --
# that is what links a commit to the account, and it keeps a personal email
# out of a public repository.
#
# Format: Canonical Name <canonical@email>  Old Name <old@email>

DuckySonadar <77309815+DuckySonadar@users.noreply.github.com> <josiahlindstrom@gmail.com>
DuckySonadar <77309815+DuckySonadar@users.noreply.github.com> <Josiah@Users-MacBook-Pro.local>

# Claude Code sessions committed under the tool's default identity. The work
# was directed by the repository owner, so authorship is theirs; Claude stays
# on the commits as a Co-Authored-By trailer, which is the accurate record and
# is not affected by this file.
DuckySonadar <77309815+DuckySonadar@users.noreply.github.com> Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
